Folio -- PDF reader for AROS
==========================

Folio uses MuPDF to display PDFs in a Zune interface. It supports text
search, copying, links and yellow highlight annotations.

INSTALLATION

Use the build for your architecture and ABI; AROS builds are not
interchangeable. Development packages include BUILD-REPORT.md with their
build and test status.

Unpack the archive anywhere and double-click the Folio icon. The icon sets
an 8 MB stack. Keep this value if you replace the icon.

From a Shell:

    Stack 8388608
    Folio [-t] [file.pdf [page]]

Quote filenames containing spaces. The optional page number starts at 1.
The -t option displays render timing and queue status. MuPDF diagnostics
go to the Shell console; a Workbench launch does not open a console.
MuPDF and its dependencies are linked into the executable. External web
links additionally require openurl.library.

OPENING AND NAVIGATION

Open a document with Project > Open, drop a PDF icon on the window, or use
Open Recent. With no document open, the start page lists recent documents.
Folio restores each document's reading position, zoom and view mode.

Single Page scrolls continuously. Magazine shows pairs 1-2, 3-4, and so on;
an odd final page is centred on its own. Selecting Magazine fits each
spread to the window. Manual zoom stops automatic fitting; Fit Page
restores it.

Previous and Next move by one page in Single Page or one spread in
Magazine. Enter a number between them and press Return to jump to a page.
An invalid entry restores the current number without moving the view.
Go to Page (Amiga+J) clears and focuses this field.

Click a Pages thumbnail or Outline entry to jump. The current thumbnail
is marked; the panel does not automatically scroll as you read. Drag the
divider to resize the sidebar. Click an underlined link to follow it.

KEYBOARD AND MOUSE

    Amiga+O          Open
    Amiga+S          Save highlights
    Amiga+A          Save As
    Amiga+Q          Quit
    Amiga+C          Copy selected text
    Amiga+I          Copy as Image
    Amiga+H          Highlight selected text
    Amiga+F          Focus Find
    Amiga+G          Find Next
    Amiga+J          Go to Page
    Amiga+1 / 2      Single Page / Magazine
    Amiga+= / -      Zoom in / out
    Amiga+0 / 9      Fit Width / Fit Page
    Amiga+R          Retry failed page renders
    Left / Right     Previous / next page or spread
    Home / End       First / last page
    Up / Down        Scroll within the view
    Page Up / Down   Scroll a screenful; turn spreads in Magazine
    Space            Scroll forward; next spread in Magazine
    Mouse wheel      Scroll; turn spreads in Magazine
    Ctrl+wheel       Zoom around the pointer (Amiga+wheel also works)

Drag over text to select it, including across pages. Right-click a page
for Copy, Copy as Image and Highlight.

SEARCH, COPY AND HIGHLIGHTS

Enter text in Find and press Return. Search starts at the current page,
wraps at the end and marks matches on the first matching page. Find Next
continues with the following page, rather than stepping through individual
matches on the same page. Scans need a text layer for search or selection;
Folio does not perform OCR.

Copy writes text as FTXT with CHRS (Latin-1) and UTF8 chunks. Programs
reading only CHRS may show substitutes or '?' for unsupported characters.
Copy as Image copies a rectangle on one page as a 24-bit ILBM.

Highlight adds yellow PDF annotations to selected text. Save appends them
to the original file when incremental saving is supported. Otherwise,
use Save As to write a separate file. Folio asks before discarding unsaved
highlights when opening another document or quitting.

SAVED SETTINGS

Reading positions and recent-file history are stored in ENV:Folio/state,
then persisted to ENVARC:Folio/state on exit. Start-page previews are stored
in the corresponding Folio/thumbs/ drawers. These do not change the PDFs.
Open Recent > Clear History clears the recent list.

LIMITATIONS

No printing, form filling, OCR, highlight removal or other annotation types.
Rendering a complex page can block the window until it finishes.
Double-click word selection is not implemented.
Copy as Image appeared blank in MultiView during AROS One testing; other
clipboard receivers were not tested.

SOURCE AND LICENCE

Folio is licensed under GNU AGPL version 3 or later; see LICENSE.
Dependency and font licences are in licenses/.

Repository: https://github.com/tomaszstaniak/aros-foliopdf
Use the source archive supplied with your binary package. It contains the
MuPDF revision in upstreams.json, local patches, and scripts/bootstrap.sh
to fetch and prepare that dependency. See docs/BUILDING.md in the source.
Changes are listed in CHANGELOG (or CHANGELOG.md in development packages).

